{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$verdictPath = '\"'C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-11-01d-leg29/WI-978-plan-critique-1.md'\n\"'$verdictText = @'\"'\nReviewed: e62eea418778b8ccf35ad484b8a484bf259d77c3\n\n### INDEPENDENT PLAN CRITIC — WI-978 single-plan decomposition — Round 1 — 2026-11-01\n\nProvenance: fresh non-author critic session invoked for coordinator leg \"'`2026-11-01d-leg29`; this session did not produce the plan or implementation. No provider session id was supplied. Read the plan directly with `git show` at the reviewed commit. No prior plan critique, implementer session notes, docs/status.md, or docs/log.md was read. The artifact is text and was inspected directly; no image proxy was needed.\n\nRubric: `docs/rubrics/plan-decomposition.md` at the reviewed commit (blob `89674a5a12463d7878348dde9d2849da4f711b63`), including G5'\"'s reference to \"'`docs/rubrics/architecture-decomposition.md` (blob `b033f489ae64851e857d0006c6efe82027ad8ccd`). Intent sources at that commit: the full `docs/work/active/wi-978/WI-978-watermark-carrier.md`, its specref `docs/plans/2026-10-11-review-churn/README.md#16-one-mint-across-parallel-lanes`, SR-174 in `docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml`, and SN-025/SN-027 in `docs/requirements/stakeholder-needs.toml`. Used the supplied 25-clause coverage report. Consulted IF-101 and the relevant landing/refresh code and coordinator landing contract to resolve concrete seams and ordering.\n\nRubric adequacy: the anchors independently cover the supplied intent at the plan tier. DevStg-Tests and B2 require real delivery of reservation uniqueness, reserved-only landing, fold preservation, keep-or-mint, and upgrade obligations; G4/B4 require an executable landing order; G5 carries the changed state, domain and input boundaries. This derivation rests on the SN/SR intent and spec, rather than on the permissiveness of a TC. No missing rubric anchor is needed for these findings.\n\nTransfer caveat: debate/selection evidence comes from QA, math and code with objective verifiers; plan-artifact quality and two-planner reconciliation remain unbenchmarked. This rubric is an extrapolation, not a proven instrument.\n\nAnchors judged: DevStg-Reqs, DevStg-Tests, DevStg-Impl, G4, G5, B1, B2, B3, B4. The steps identify concrete deliverables and checks; the reported multi-coverage generally separates implementation, callers, documentation and final verification. No seam duplication or padding finding is raised. `DELTA: within` is supported: P1/P2/P5/P12 carry the carrier state and record domain, and P1/P6/P7/P8 carry the new landing input and IF-101 requestors (A2/A3/A4/A6). The findings below concern honest coverage and buildable order.\n\nFindings:\n- [MAJOR] DevStg-Tests/B2 (F1) -> P7, P8 and P12, coverage of D12'\"'s landing fold: P7 folds only during station refresh; P8's supported hand-squash route reads the index and validates reservations, with no fold into the staged landing. A lane can reserve and fold its own range, another lane can then reserve a further range, and the first lane's hand squash passes the planned check while omitting the later carrier marks and records. The landing therefore does not deliver the required per-space maximum and record union, despite D12 being marked covered. -> Carry the carrier fold into the hand-squash landing procedure or implementation, with the folded watermark included in the judged staged tree; add a hand-squash case where the carrier advances after the lane's earlier fold and assert the landed marks and records include it. -> @planner\n- [MAJOR] G4/B4 (F2) -> P13 -> P14 -> P15 -> P16: P13 judges the new LLR/TC rows and takes their acts, but P15 performs the final rebase and explicitly permits renumbering those same rows when the actual reserved ranges differ. Concurrent lanes advancing the LLR/TC floors before this lane's final reservation are a normal supported case. P13's instruction to repeat a sitting when a rebase changes a row does not cover the subsequent P15 renumbering. The DAG reaches landing after changing already-judged and acted-on rows, contrary to the existing landing contract that a renumbered row counts as changed and must be re-sat before the final act. -> Place self-reservation and any renumbering before the final checkpoint/act, or explicitly add the conditional re-sitting and final act after P15; make P16 depend on approval of the final numbered rows and keep the final act after the final rebase. -> @planner\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=2\n'@\n[System.IO.Directory]::CreateDirectory([System.IO.Path]::GetDirectoryName(\"'$verdictPath)) | Out-Null\n[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($verdictPath, $verdictText + \"`n\", [System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false))\nGet-Content -LiteralPath $verdictPath -TotalCount 3\nGet-Content -LiteralPath $verdictPath -Tail 1'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
